Package: RSYC
Title: Remote Sensing-Derived Yield Curves for Canada
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    c(
    person(given = "Piotr", 
           family = "Tompalski",
           email = "piotr.tompalski@NRCan-RNCan.gc.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person(paste("His Majesty the King in Right of Canada,",
                 "as represented by the Minister of Natural Resources Canada"),
           role = "cph")
    )
Description: Provides published remote sensing-based yield curves for
    aboveground biomass and total volume across Canada, as described in
    Tompalski et al. (2024) <doi:10.1016/j.foreco.2024.121894> and
    Tompalski et al. (2025) <doi:10.1093/forestry/cpaf067>. Models are
    available for 150 km tiles and four levels of Canada's ecological land
    classification. Functions help users find curves by species and area,
    estimate yield at a given stand age, calibrate curves to local
    observations, and build spatial yield-curve datasets.
